WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.544
Week twelve.

00:00:01.594 --> 00:00:05.088
Measuring what matters, with Nicky Barton from Mutinex.

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:08.708
Last-click attribution gives the final click all the credit.

00:00:08.758 --> 00:00:12.380
It's like a group assignment where whoever hits submit gets the whole mark.

00:00:12.967 --> 00:00:13.767
Crediting only the bottom of the funnel starves the brand.

00:00:13.737 --> 00:00:18.553
Then privacy changes broke individual tracking.

00:00:18.603 --> 00:00:20.517
Ask every platform what it sold,

00:00:20.567 --> 00:00:23.319
and the answers add up to more than a hundred percent.

00:00:23.933 --> 00:00:30.033
Marketing mix modelling reads the whole market: sales, spend, price, seasonality and competitors.

00:00:30.083 --> 00:00:33.613
It shows what drove sales, and where the next dollar should go.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.612
It thinks in pictures.

00:00:35.662 --> 00:00:36.462
A café on a busy corner is your baseline.

00:00:36.354 --> 00:00:38.168
A song stuck in your head: ads keep working.

00:00:38.218 --> 00:00:44.264
And the fifth slice of pizza: diminishing returns.

00:00:44.867 --> 00:00:48.667
Across eighty three brands, those that kept their brand muscle grew most.

00:00:48.717 --> 00:00:51.571
If you can't add budget, don't add channels.

00:00:52.167 --> 00:00:53.244
The takeaway?

00:00:53.294 --> 00:00:54.974
Judgement becomes the job.

00:00:55.024 --> 00:00:57.695
Always ask: how do we know it worked?
